ThreadSanitizer sees a fiber's mutex only as the atomics of its spinlock:
it follows their ordering, so a race on what the mutex guards is still
found, but it cannot tell the mutex is one -- which mutexes were held where
a race is reported, the order they are taken in, one destroyed while held.
Where Boost.Context reports each fiber to it (BOOST_USE_TSAN), each mutex
is told to it now, through its mutex annotations: at the moment a fiber
comes to hold it and the moment it lets it go, under the spinlock, back to
back, so that nothing of the spinlock or the wait queue is hidden from it.
A try_lock and a timed lock are told as tries, which may not deadlock, and
the recursive mutexes as reentrant. The condition variable lets its mutex
go and takes it again through them. Without BOOST_USE_TSAN nothing changes.

diff --git a/include/boost/fiber/detail/tsan.hpp b/include/boost/fiber/detail/tsan.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..62358c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/boost/fiber/detail/tsan.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+//          Distributed under the Boost Software License, Version 1.0.
+//    (See accompanying file LICENSE_1_0.txt or copy at
+//          http://www.boost.org/LICENSE_1_0.txt)
+
+#ifndef BOOST_FIBERS_DETAIL_TSAN_H
+#define BOOST_FIBERS_DETAIL_TSAN_H
+
+// ThreadSanitizer's mutex annotations, where Boost.Context reports each
+// fiber to it (BOOST_USE_TSAN): a fiber's mutex is told to it as a mutex at
+// the moment a fiber comes to hold it and the moment it lets it go, under
+// the mutex's spinlock. The spinlock and the wait queue stay as TSan sees
+// them otherwise, atomics and all; what the annotations add is the mutex
+// itself -- which are held where a race is reported, the order they are
+// taken in, one destroyed while held.
+
+#if defined(BOOST_USE_TSAN)
+# include <sanitizer/tsan_interface.h>
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_ACQUIRED(m, flags) \
+    ( __tsan_mutex_pre_lock( (m), (flags) ), __tsan_mutex_post_lock( (m), (flags), 0) )
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_RELEASED(m) \
+    ( __tsan_mutex_pre_unlock( (m), 0), __tsan_mutex_post_unlock( (m), 0) )
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_DESTROYED(m) __tsan_mutex_destroy( (m), 0)
+// a try_lock, and a timed lock, which may not deadlock
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_TRY __tsan_mutex_try_lock
+// a recursive mutex, which its holder takes again
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_REENTRANT __tsan_mutex_write_reentrant
+#else
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_ACQUIRED(m, flags) ((void) 0)
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_RELEASED(m) ((void) 0)
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_DESTROYED(m) ((void) 0)
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_TRY 0
+# define BOOST_FIBERS_TSAN_REENTRANT 0
+#endif
+
+#endif // BOOST_FIBERS_DETAIL_TSAN_H
